- Method: fresh public internet research only. Research steps attempted and their outcomes: a direct fetch of `benchlm.ai/md/models/exo-free.md` (**404**); two targeted searches, the first of which returned only two results and the second of which surfaced the full discovery trail; and reads of Pi's model-details page (the `exo-free` / `opencode` / `openai-completions` registration, the `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1` base URL, **text and image input, reasoning yes, context window 1,048,576, max tokens 131,072**), Free AI Credits' offer page (**$0 input, output and cached reads**, "available for a limited time, with no end date stated", and the data-collection warning), TypingMind's pricing calculator (the attachments / reasoning / tool-calling / image-input capability list and the $0.00 rates), ArtificialWatch's automated radar entry (catalog id `opencode/exo-free`, **first observed 2026-10-06 22:54 UTC** via models.dev), two X posts establishing the **2026-10-06 ~22:30 anonymous drop**, the "reasoning only on high" detail, the "Lab unknown. Free while they collect feedback" characterization and the **competing claim that the backend is "not a model, but a router with Claude and GPT inside"**, and Free AI API's 2026-10-07 hands-on review, which supplied the **lm.ikale.io 99.4% Claude Opus 5.5 fingerprint** (with claude-fable-5.1 at 0.4%), the fingerprinting methodology (~300 pseudo-random numbers plus tokenizer boundary probes), **its own critique of that evidence as closed-set matching that cannot distinguish a model from its distillate**, the three competing theories (NDA blind evaluation, routing misconfiguration, Opus-distilled open-weights model), the Zen `/v1/models` registration confirmation, the qualitative Pelican-on-a-Bicycle and convenience-store Blender test reports, the multimodal diagnosis report, the **absence of zero-data-retention guarantees with prompts and screenshots used for training**, and the documented **`Endpoint is unavailable` notices and 429 rate limits**. **No benchmark figure of any kind was found for this identifier**, and that is stated rather than implied. **The 99.4% fingerprint is explicitly refused as a basis for importing Claude Opus 5.5's benchmark suite**, on three stated grounds — the publishing source itself explains the metric is closed-set and cannot separate identity from distillation, a credible competing claim describes a multi-model router, and Theory B (transient routing misconfiguration) would mean the observed behaviour is not stable — applying the same standard used earlier in this queue for `omen-alpha` (behavioural impressions and self-identification are not attribution) and `owl-alpha` (another folder's benchmarks must not be imported). The qualitative Blender and Pelican results are described in full and deliberately **not** converted into scores, since they are single-tester, single-attempt, unscored anecdotes without published prompts, pass rates, baselines or reproduction. No data was imported from any other folder, and no peer `model/` findings files were read. The model's two-day age is named as the primary cause of the evidence gap, and reversal criteria are stated so the exclusion is auditable and short-lived.
